      <memberdef kind="function" id="group__isotp__protocol_1ga29356e99657bbe884b0a15a5eedfcbce" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>int</type>
        <definition>int isotp_decode</definition>
        <argsstring>(const uint8_t *frame, size_t length, struct isotp_pdu *pdu)</argsstring>
        <name>isotp_decode</name>
        <param>
          <type>const uint8_t *</type>
          <declname>frame</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>size_t</type>
          <declname>length</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>struct <ref refid="structisotp__pdu" kindref="compound">isotp_pdu</ref> *</type>
          <declname>pdu</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Validate one received CAN frame and describe it. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Rejects frames that ISO 15765-2 tells a receiver to ignore: unknown frame type, SF_DL of 0 or longer than the frame, a First Frame that is not 8 bytes long or announces a message that would fit a Single Frame (or, with the 32-bit FF_DL, fits the 12-bit field), a Consecutive Frame without data, a Flow Control frame shorter than 3 bytes. The flow status is not checked here: an unknown value is an N_INVALID_FS condition the sender has to report. <parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>frame</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>CAN frame data. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>length</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>CAN data length, 1..8. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>pdu</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Receives the description. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<parameterlist kind="retval"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>ISOTP_OK</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para><computeroutput>pdu</computeroutput> describes a valid frame. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>ISOTP_ERROR</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>NULL argument, invalid length or malformed frame. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
