    <briefdescription>
<para>Pure functions that translate between CAN frames and ISO-TP PDUs. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The codec holds no state. <ref refid="group__isotp__protocol_1ga29356e99657bbe884b0a15a5eedfcbce" kindref="member">isotp_decode</ref> validates one received CAN frame and describes it in a <ref refid="structisotp__pdu" kindref="compound">isotp_pdu</ref>; the encoders write one frame into a caller buffer and return its length. Frames are classical CAN (up to 8 data bytes) with normal addressing. The encoders produce the shortest frame; <ref refid="group__isotp__protocol_1ga088e0db8cacc79d076e9326232f130c5" kindref="member">isotp_frame_pad</ref> fills it up to 8 bytes when the bus requires padding.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="par"><title>Public interface includes:</title><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Decoding: <ref refid="group__isotp__protocol_1ga29356e99657bbe884b0a15a5eedfcbce" kindref="member">isotp_decode</ref>. </para>
</listitem>
<listitem><para>Encoding: <ref refid="group__isotp__protocol_1gac803d6e1a34aa390e7479ad62a76a497" kindref="member">isotp_encode_single</ref>, <ref refid="group__isotp__protocol_1ga366f66f9e9f6b1b2e9da2f93605ee8ec" kindref="member">isotp_encode_first</ref>, <ref refid="group__isotp__protocol_1gab00b72cee8a6c7d9c63c94d6d279ec71" kindref="member">isotp_encode_consecutive</ref>, <ref refid="group__isotp__protocol_1gaa83fd08cc39152dfec534c289da9a1fa" kindref="member">isotp_encode_flow_control</ref>, <ref refid="group__isotp__protocol_1ga088e0db8cacc79d076e9326232f130c5" kindref="member">isotp_frame_pad</ref>. </para>
</listitem>
<listitem><para>Separation time: <ref refid="group__isotp__protocol_1gad1a866dca4cfd61976f9066ac315707a" kindref="member">isotp_st_min_encode</ref>, <ref refid="group__isotp__protocol_1ga0cf4df17204718dd2d255a328b1c6508" kindref="member">isotp_st_min_decode</ref>. </para>
</listitem>
</itemizedlist>
</para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
